    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "file header comment",
      "prov:value": "The engine keeps the work context; no step carries work-plan markup. Bean xies. Six stages between \"the graph is in the repository\" and \"a reader's browser has the bytes\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "file header comment",
      "prov:value": "The owner stated the ingestion method as undetermined — \"ingestion method not determined\" — so the diagram reaches a decision and stops there rather than naming a transport."
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "file header comment",
      "prov:value": "It is what `A_Distribute` may put in front of the origin, which is why the publish-target lane holds one activity and not two: modelling the cache as a participant makes its URL look like the published one, and the published URL is a promise — bean xies calls the consequence \"EXTREME care in URL handling\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "task D_Constraints",
      "prov:value": "Say which figures were measured, which were quoted from a vendor, and which could not be obtained — a figure from a chat message is none of the three, and the who-iris catalogue carries the worked example where \"0.7 TB\" propagated through ten files and the measured figure was about half."
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "serviceTask S_Sign",
      "prov:value": "THE TRUST ANCHOR IS GDHCN, SPECIFIED BY THE WHO SMART TRUST IG (owner, 2026-09-20, paraphrased: proposal signing is GDHCN, as the WHO SMART Trust IG specifies). READ OFF THAT IG rather than from general knowledge: a GDHCN trustlist distributes KEY MATERIAL as W3C DID documents, and says nothing about what you wrap your bytes in — the health-certificate envelope is a separate specification in the same IG, and a document package is not a health certificate.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "task E_HumanEyes",
      "prov:value": "Bean xies, gate 3, and the one that is easy to drop because gate 2 (merge to main) looks like an approval. It is not: merging approves the CHANGE, and this approves what a reader will actually see. continual-progress measured why a description cannot stand in for it (PR #178, 2026-09-16).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xies",
        "#178",
        "2026-09-16",
        "PR #178"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "exclusiveGateway GW_Transport",
      "prov:value": "THIS GATEWAY HAS NO DEFAULT BRANCH, AND THAT IS THE POINT. Owner, 2026-09-20: \"ingestion method not determined.\" Pull from the portal, push to an object store, a git fetch, a signed tarball on a schedule — they differ in cost, in who initiates, in what must be reachable from where, and in what happens when a publication is missed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "serviceTask A_Distribute",
      "prov:value": "Uploading and exposing are separable steps on purpose (xies, gate 4), because collapsing them removes the last moment at which a bad URL layout can still be caught.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xies"
